  "name": "motor-thermal",
  "$comment": "Thermal domain example: a 24 V DC motor (DCMotorThermal: R = 2 Ohm at 293.15 K, copper alpha = 0.00393 1/K, k_t = 0.05 N*m/A) drives a fan inertia (2e-4 kg*m^2) against a viscous drag (4e-4 N*m*s/rad). The copper loss i^2*R(T) leaves the winding port as heat flow into the winding capacity (30 J/K), conducts through the insulation (1.5 W/K) into the housing (150 J/K) and leaves by convection (h = 20 W/(m^2*K), A = 0.05 m^2) to a 293.15 K ambient. Three series HeatFlowSensors and three Integrators record the heat flows and their energies for the first-law checks.",
